'''Lanais''' were an [[Bird|avian]] [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] who lived on [[Temple Island]] on the [[ocean]] [[planet]] of [[Ahch-To]] for [[Millennium|thousands]] of [[Standard year|years]]. The [[Gender|females]] of the species took on the role of [[Caretakers]] and attended to the [[Jedi village|ancient structures]] on the [[Temple Island|sacred island]]&mdash;which was the site of the [[first Jedi Temple]], where [[Jedi Master]] [[Luke Skywalker]] came to live as a hermit after his [[Jedi]] students were [[Destruction of the Jedi Temple|killed]] by his nephew [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]]&mdash;while the males were known as the [[Visitors]].

==Biology and appearance==
[[Homeworld|Native]] to the [[Water|aquatic]] [[planet]] [[Ahch-To]],<ref name="Episode VIII" /> Lanais were an [[Bird|avian]] [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] who dwelled on [[Temple Island]] which held the [[first Jedi Temple]]. They evolved from the same evolutionary stock of seabirds that produced the [[porg]]s,<ref name="TLJVD" /> and were distinguished by their [[Color|gray]] skin and [[bird]]-like skinny [[Limb|feet]].<ref name="Episode VIII" /> Innate water-shedding ability of their skin, hair, and plumage afforded by natural oils allowed Lanais to withstand intense conditions of their oceanic planet. They possessed salt glands that assisted in the extraction of sea salt from their sustenance, as well as membranes which closed over their eyes, enabling sharp underwater vision.<ref name="TLJVD" />

==Society and culture==
Lanais spoke the non-[[Galactic Basic Standard|Basic]] [[language]] of the [[Lanai's language|same name]],<ref name="Episode VIII" /> which was combination of spoken words and hand motions.<ref name="TLJVD" /> They were able to communicate with [[Jedi Master]] [[Luke Skywalker]] during his self-imposed [[Exile (punishment)|exile]] on Ahch-To.<ref name="Episode VIII" /> Written language, which consisted of cuneiform marks based on the shape of their feet, was rare, and fire signals were preferred for long-range communications.<ref name="TLJVD" />

To keep rhythm during their repetitive chores, their culture was intrinsically musical. [[Lanai-song]] was a mix of whistles and guttural oscillations that echo from their village and worksites. The Lanais' technology was solely derived from fish; useful skins and skeletons were gathered during their fishing in the bountiful oceans of their homeworld.<ref name="TLJVD" />

==History==
[[File:CaretakerVillage-SoH.png|thumb|left|250px|Caretakers attend to their duties in their village.]]
For [[Millennium|thousands]] of [[Standard year|years]], Lanais inhabited the Temple Island on Ahch-To, and the female Caretakers tended to the ancient structures at the site of the first [[Jedi temple]].<ref name="TLJVD" /> After the [[Destruction of the Jedi Temple|death]] of his [[Jedi]] students at the hands of his former [[Padawan|apprentice]] and nephew [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]], the legendary Jedi Master Luke Skywalker came to Ahch-To,<ref name="Episode VII">{{Film|VII}}</ref> the [[Homeworld|home]] of the Lanais,<ref name="Look and Find" /> to live in solitude.<ref name="Episode VII" /> The Jedi Master's presence on the island was accepted and tolerated by the Lanais, but when [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] came to the island to be [[Jedi training|trained]] by him, the Caretakers found that she disrupted their work.<ref name="Episode VIII" /> On one occasion, Rey [[Telekinesis|lifted]] two Lanai [[Force power|using]] [[the Force]] out of frustration before she put them back down.<ref name="Life Lessons">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=26|story=Life Lessons}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|They're kind of these sort of fish-bird type aliens who live on the island. They've been there for thousands of years, and they essentially keep up the structures on the island.|Rian Johnson|<ref name="EW">{{WebCite|url=http://ew.com/movies/2017/08/09/star-wars-last-jedi-porgs-caretakers|text=''The Last Jedi'': Meet the porgs and 'The Caretakers' from Luke Skywalker's island|author=Breznican, Anthony|date=2017-08-09|work=[[Wikipedia:Entertainment Weekly|Entertainment Weekly]]|archivedate=20170814205151}}</ref>}}
The Lanais were created and developed for the [[2017]] ''[[Star Wars]]'' saga film [[Star Wars: Episode VIII The Last Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VIII ''The Last Jedi'']].<ref name="Episode VIII" /> The Caretakers were first revealed in an article by [[Entertainment Weekly Books|''Entertainment Weekly'']], released on [[August 9]], 2017.<ref name="EW" />

[[Rian Johnson]], the writer and director of ''The Last Jedi'', wanted the Lanais to bear resemblance to [[Wikipedia:Nun|nunnery]] in real life. They were designed by [[Neal Scanlan]]'s crew. Concept artist [[Jake Lunt Davies]] made multiple different designs of their physiology which were morphed together into the final design.<ref name=":0">{{SW|url=news/designing-star-wars-the-last-jedi-part-2-creating-the-caretakers|text=Designing ''Star Wars: The Last Jedi'', Part 2: Creating the Caretakers}}</ref> [[Michael Kaplan]] made their working costumes which reflected "a nun-like, spartan sort of existence."<ref name="EW" /> [[Martin Rezard]] was the lead sculptor.<ref name=":0" />

Johnson also described their language as "a blubbery sort of Scottish fish talk."<ref name="EW" /> The creature effects supervisor Neal Scanlan also said that he felt like "the only creatures that would ever exist on the Ahch-To island were those indigenous to it, where very few other species and [[DNA]] would have reached them." This led Scanlan to the idea of the Lanais being an extrapolation from the [[porg]]s<ref name="Empire">{{WebCite|url=https://www.empireonline.com/movies/star-wars-last-jedi/last-jedi-new-revelations-star-wars-creatures-boss|text=The Last Jedi: New Revelations From Star Wars Creatures Boss|author=Nugent, John|date=2017-10-30|work=[[Wikipedia:Empire (film magazine)|Empire]]|archivedate=20171031174135}}</ref>&mdash;a sea [[bird]] species native to Ahch-To<ref name="Porg">{{SW|url=news/introducing-porgs-the-cute-new-creatures-from-star-wars-the-last-jedi|text=Introducing Porgs, the Cute New Creatures from ''Star Wars: The Last Jedi''}}</ref>&mdash;and having bird-like feet, despite being a further developed race.<ref name="Empire" />

During the film's production, the Lanais were animated with a person inside, one of whom was a friend of [[Daisy Ridley]],<ref name="EW" /> the actress who portrays the character Rey in the film.<ref name="Episode VIII" />

During the development of [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']], Lanai were at one point going to appear as a group of [[assassin]]s on [[Kijimi]].<ref name="Art of TROS">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker]]''</ref>

